Chapter: CharOrderRefused
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ordering a character is refused at CHECK. Unlike the Text case this one is
 well defined and misleads instead: CCE numbers characters by English letter
 frequency, so 'd' is 22 and 'b' is 32 and `'d' < 'b'` answered True. Code
 that wants code-point arithmetic writes char-code and compares Integers,
 which says what it is doing.

 The Text case is a separate file, so that neither refusal can stand in for
 the other.

Section: Refused

  bad-lt : Boolean
  bad-lt = 'd' < 'b'

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show bad-lt)
  end

